reference[24]: "Commands: create (up), adopt, orphans, list (ls, ps, who), extend, release (down), sweep, job,","env, setup hooks, agent (internal SSH protocol), machine install.","Global flags: --axi (agents), --json (scripts), --help. No --human flag.",Human output on terminals; AXI when DIBS_AXI=1 or stdout is not a TTY.,"--axi and --json are mutually exclusive; either overrides DIBS_AXI.","Version: --version, -v, -V.","Environment: DIBS_OWNER; DIBS_STATE (default $XDG_STATE_HOME/dibs or",~/.local/state/dibs). State is local to one host and one Unix user.,"Examples:","  dibs","  dibs create --adapter kind --ttl 1h --resources '2 CPUs, test lab'","  dibs sweep --confirm",Run dibs <command> --help for command flags.,"Output: --axi for agents, --json for scripts (mutually exclusive).","Default: human on terminals; AXI for pipes or DIBS_AXI=1.","Lease commands: --full restores complete AXI records/text; JSON is always complete.","","Exit codes: 0 success (including no-ops), 1 operation failed, 2 invalid usage.","dibs job: child's exit code on completion; 124 deadline killed child;",75 (EX_TEMPFAIL) no slot within wait. Dibs's own 1/2 apply only when no child,was started. Signal termination returns 128 + signal number. Helper/wait,failures after start use 125/126 and diagnostics on stderr.,76 is SSH transport/protocol failure with unknown remote result (stderr).,Child exit 255 is preserved and is not confused with SSH failure.
usage: "dibs: owner-and-expiry leases for local resources (macOS and Linux)."
